abstract: >-
  Deterministic evaluation harness and four-layer blameless incident postmortem
  framework for humanoid robot Sim-to-Real deployment pipelines (Isaac Gym /
  MuJoCo -> Interface Protocol -> Unitree G1 Hardware). Reconstructs
  timestamp-verified incident timelines from multi-source telemetry logs and
  attributes Sim-to-Real failures across four orthogonal layers: (1) Simulation
  Environment (contact physics, terrain, sensor noise), (2) Interface Protocol
  (frame rate, coordinate transforms, unit/version mismatch), (3) Hardware &
  Safety (joint limits, thermal/current protection, communication drop, E-stop
  gates), and (4) Model Policy (out-of-distribution states, action bounds,
  reward/observation design).
